      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For heavy industrial loads with uneven weight distribution, you must treat the center of gravity with the utmost care, especially in high-density racking. It's crucial to center the load as much as possible within the pallet footprint, even if the contents are lopsided. If the weight is heavily skewed, you might need to employ specialized bracing or use smaller, more stable stacking units instead of relying on the original pallet configuration. Always consult your racking manufacturer's load charts for maximum permissible eccentric loading.",
