    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense about the lateral shifting. One thing that's been bugging the floor supervisors is that we occasionally have stacks that seem perfectly fine, but then suddenly one pallet ends up slightly out of alignment or skewed, like someone bumped it or it just moved on its own. Is there any way to account for that kind of random instability in the stacking plan, or is that just part of the risk in high-density warehousing?",
